---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — CaloriesAI (Nori)"
  description="Privacy Policy for CaloriesAI mobile app. Last updated March 2026."
>
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 text-gray-200">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-10">Last updated: March 2026</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 leading-relaxed text-gray-300">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>CaloriesAI ("we", "us", or "our") is committed to protecting your privacy in compliance with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and Spanish data protection law (LOPDGDD). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard your information when you use the CaloriesAI mobile application.</p>
        <p class="mt-2"><strong>Data Controller:</strong> CaloriesAI — <a href="mailto:sirdanielsan64manager@gmail.com" class="text-blue-400 underline">sirdanielsan64manager@gmail.com</a> (España / Spain)</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="font-medium text-gray-200 mb-1">a) Information you provide directly:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 mb-3">
          <li>Profile data (name, age, height, weight, fitness goals)</li>
          <li>Meal entries and food logs</li>
          <li>Weight measurements and progress photos</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="font-medium text-gray-200 mb-1">b) Health data (with your permission):</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 mb-3">
          <li>Step count, active energy, and heart rate from Apple Health</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="font-medium text-gray-200 mb-1">c) Automatically collected information:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li>App crash reports and diagnostic data (anonymised, via Sentry)</li>
          <li>Aggregate usage statistics (no personally identifiable information)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">3. How We Use Your Data</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li>To provide core app functionality (calorie tracking, meal logging, progress charts)</li>
          <li>To generate personalised AI meal plans and nutrition analysis</li>
          <li>To send local push notifications you have configured</li>
          <li>To back up your data to iCloud when you enable this feature</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">4. Data Storage</h2>
        <p>All meal, health, and weight data is stored locally on your device. If you enable iCloud Sync, data is backed up to your personal iCloud account and is encrypted by Apple. We do not operate our own servers for personal data storage.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">5. AI Analysis</h2>
        <p>When you use photo or text analysis features, your input is sent to a third-party AI provider for processing and returned immediately. Photos and text descriptions are not stored by CaloriesAI or the AI provider after the analysis response is returned.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">6. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p class="mb-2"><strong>a) AI Provider:</strong> Photo and text analysis features rely on a third-party AI API. Data sent for analysis is subject to the provider's data processing terms, which prohibit retention of user content.</p>
        <p class="mb-2"><strong>b) Sentry (Crash Reporting):</strong> We use Sentry (sentry.io) to collect anonymous crash reports and error logs. These contain no personally identifiable information and are used solely to improve app stability.</p>
        <p><strong>c) Apple iCloud:</strong> If you enable iCloud Sync, your data is backed up to your personal Apple iCloud account and governed by Apple's Privacy Policy.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">7. Data Sharing</h2>
        <p>We do not sell, trade, or rent your personal information to third parties. We do not share your data with advertisers or marketing platforms.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">8. Your Rights (GDPR / LOPDGDD)</h2>
        <p class="mb-2">Under EU and Spanish data protection law, you have the following rights:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Right of access:</strong> export your data via Settings → Export Data → Export User Data (GDPR)</li>
          <li><strong>Right to rectification:</strong> correct your data via Settings → Account</li>
          <li><strong>Right to erasure:</strong> Settings → Account → Delete Account</li>
          <li><strong>Right to data portability:</strong> JSON export via Settings → Export Data</li>
          <li><strong>Right to object / restrict processing:</strong> contact us at sirdanielsan64manager@gmail.com</li>
          <li><strong>Right to lodge a complaint:</strong> <a href="https://www.aepd.es" class="text-blue-400 underline" target="_blank">Agencia Española de Protección de Datos (AEPD)</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:sirdanielsan64manager@gmail.com" class="text-blue-400 underline">sirdanielsan64manager@gmail.com</a>. We will respond within 30 days as required by GDPR Article 12.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">9. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>CaloriesAI is not intended for use by children under 13 years of age. We do not knowingly collect data from children.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of significant changes within the app.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">11. Contact</h2>
        <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or wish to exercise your data rights:</p>
        <p class="mt-1"><a href="mailto:sirdanielsan64manager@gmail.com" class="text-blue-400 underline">sirdanielsan64manager@gmail.com</a></p>
        <p class="mt-1">Supervisory Authority (España): <a href="https://www.aepd.es" class="text-blue-400 underline" target="_blank">Agencia Española de Protección de Datos (AEPD)</a></p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
